      "SetLogger.jsx (manage view, \"add\" picker): createCustomFooter's onPick for the multi-select Add Exercises screen was `addExercise`, which commits straight to the workout via addWorkoutExercise and then calls closePicker() -- closePicker resets pickerFor to null and clears pickerMultiSelected, so any exercises already checked in the batch were silently discarded the moment a custom exercise got created. handleCreateCustomExercise itself never closes anything (CustomExerciseModal's onClose only toggles showCreateCustom off), so the fix was just changing what gets called on creation: `createCustomFooter((l) => togglePickerSelect(l))` adds the new normalized exercise into pickerMultiSelected instead of committing it, leaving prior picks untouched and the Add Exercises screen still open with the new custom exercise now visible (and pre-checked) in the list. The single-exercise replace picker (`createCustomFooter((l) => replaceExercise(i, l))`) is unaffected -- immediate commit is correct there since there's only ever one exercise being picked.",
