      "SetLogger.jsx: newItem carries warmupRestSeconds alongside restSeconds. New adjustWarmupRest(i, seconds) mirrors adjustRest's null-if-matches-global-default storage logic. Manage view: a second \"Warmup rest timer\" +/- control renders directly under the existing \"Rest timer\" row, gated on (w.plannedWarmup || 0) > 0 so it only appears for exercises that actually have planned warmup sets. saveSet()'s post-log countdown now branches on the just-logged set's isWarmup flag -- `isWarmup ? (ex.warmupRestSeconds || getPrefs().warmupRestSeconds) : (ex.restSeconds || getPrefs().restSeconds)` -- instead of always using the working-set value. applyRestToAll now also nulls out warmupRestSeconds for every exercise (and passes null for both args to saveExerciseDefaults) so \"Apply to all\" clears both overrides together, not just the working-set one.",
      "Preferences.jsx: added a \"Default warmup rest timer\" control paralleling \"Default rest timer\" in both the grouped Training Preferences sub-screen and the ungrouped in-workout quick menu layout, plus a warmupRestSeconds search keyword entry. Home.jsx: new warmupRestDefault state (mirrors restDefault) wired into the controlled Preferences instance's value/onChange so the Settings screen's copy of the pref stays in sync the same way restSeconds already does.",
      "Fixed the manage screen's new back button dropping users into the live \"workout\" view when building a workout from scratch. Root cause: workoutId/the workout_exercises rows are created immediately as exercises are added (addWorkoutExercise), but the app has no other concept of an active session -- so once workout.length > 0 the earlier `if (workout.length === 0)` empty-workout screen (which has its own no-confirm-needed delete-and-go-home back button) stops matching, and manage's back button routed straight to setView(\"workout\") same as Done, which reads as the workout having started. New manageFromScratch state, set true only by the empty-workout screen's \"Add exercises manually\" button (false when entering manage via the active workout's \"Edit Workout\" button, and cleared by finishEditing once the user commits normally via Done) distinguishes the two paths. handleManageBack: if manageFromScratch is false, behaves exactly like before (finishEditing, back to the workout view). If true and nothing has been added yet (workout.length === 0 and no pending pickerMultiSelected picks), silently deletes the workout and returns home, same as the empty-workout screen's own back button. If true and something has been added, shows a new confirm overlay (same visual pattern as the existing \"Cancel workout\" confirm) before calling handleDiscardNewWorkout, which deletes the workout row, clears session state, and calls onFinished() -- exercises picked but not yet committed via \"Add N exercises\" are included in the confirm's count alongside already-added ones.",
      "New Rest Timers subsection in Training Preferences, gating the warmup-vs-working rest distinction behind a single master toggle instead of it always being on. lib/prefs.js: new warmupRestEnabled default (true, so existing behavior for anyone already relying on per-exercise warmup rest times doesn't change on upgrade). Preferences.jsx: new local ToggleSwitch component (a literal sliding on/off control, distinct from the segmented PillRow buttons used for multi-option prefs elsewhere) since no switch component existed yet. Both the grouped Training Preferences sub-screen and the ungrouped in-workout quick menu layout now wrap the existing Default rest timer / Default warmup rest timer controls in a \"REST TIMERS\" labeled subsection with the toggle at top -- when off, only a single \"Default rest timer\" control shows (relabeled from \"Default working set rest timer\"); when on, both defaults show as before. Home.jsx: new warmupRestEnabled state (mirrors restDefault/warmupRestDefault) wired into the controlled Preferences instance.",
      "SetLogger.jsx: manage view's per-exercise \"Warmup rest timer\" control is now gated on `getPrefs().warmupRestEnabled && (w.plannedWarmup || 0) > 0` instead of just the planned-warmup check, so it disappears entirely (falling back to a single per-exercise \"Rest timer\" control) when the master toggle is off. saveSet()'s post-log countdown similarly only pulls the warmup-specific duration when `getPrefs().warmupRestEnabled` is true, otherwise always using the working-set rest value regardless of the set's isWarmup flag. No changes to the underlying exercise_defaults storage -- per-exercise warmupRestSeconds values already saved are preserved and simply re-appear if the toggle is turned back on.",
