      "ExerciseLibraryView.jsx: new ExerciseDefaultsEditor component lets any signed-in user edit their personal exercise_defaults row (machine setup -- Seat height/Bar height/Cable height/Arm setting/_machineNotes -- plus the per-exercise custom setup_fields and the freeform note) from the exercise detail sheet, with no active workout required. Reuses the exact same fetchExerciseDefaults/saveExerciseDefaults calls and setup-field semantics (numeric-vs-text toggle via `${field}__text`) as SetLogger.jsx's mid-workout editor -- same exercise_defaults row either way, so a change made from the library shows up mid-workout and vice versa. Gated on the userId prop already passed into ExerciseLibraryView from Home.jsx.",
      "lib/queries.js: new fetchExerciseHistory(userId, exerciseId), following fetchExercisePRBaselines' workouts!inner join pattern but keeping completed_at per row instead of collapsing to a single baseline. lib/volume.js: new summarizeExerciseHistory(rows) turns those rows into three raw daily series (top set weight, total working reps, total volume) merging same-day workouts; new bucketSeries(points, rangeKey, field, mode) generalizes bucketWeightHistory/bucketDailyVolume's widen-as-range-grows bucketing (7d daily, 30d by calendar week, 90d by 14-day window, 365d by month) to any single-field series with an avg or sum aggregation mode, rather than writing a third bespoke bucketing function.",
